## Rule CP-1 — No Ghost Features

Every feature listed in CHANGELOG.md must have corresponding working code, tests, and (if applicable) documentation. Do not add CHANGELOG entries for code that does not yet exist.

## Rule CP-2 — Test Coverage Floor

Every new or modified Python module must maintain >= 80% test coverage. New modules must have > 0% coverage before merge. Verify with:
```
python -m pytest tests/ --cov=devolaflow --cov-report=term-missing
```

## Rule CP-3 — Version Bump Protocol

When bumping the version, update ALL locations consistently using `scripts/bump_version.py`. The script performs 7 pattern replacements across the canonical files, then invokes `scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py` to bytewise-mirror the canonical skill into `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/`. After bumping, run `python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v` to verify all 11 locations + the stamp agree.

The canonical list of 11 synced locations is defined in rule SF-3 (`skill-format-rules.mdc`); the source of truth is `src/devolaflow/__init__.py`. For reference, the files touched are:

**Canonical (pattern-replaced by `bump_version.py`):**

1. `src/devolaflow/__init__.py` — `__version__` (source of truth)
2. `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` — frontmatter `version:`, banner, and body "Current version:" text
3. `workflow-system/agent/workflow-skill.yaml` — identity section
4. `pyproject.toml` — `version` field
5. `scripts/generate_human_docs.py` — `SOURCE_VERSION`
6. `tests/test_smoke.py` — version assertion
7. `README.md` — badge and version example
8. `workflow-system/human/demo/benchmark-results/index.html` — `SAMPLE_DATA.version`

**Project-local mirror (auto-synced by `sync_cursor_skill.py`):**

9. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/SKILL.md` — bytewise mirror of (2)
10. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/references/*.md` — 8 bytewise mirrors of `workflow-system/agent/references/*.md`
11. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/examples/*.md` — 3 bytewise mirrors of `workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md`
12. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/.devola-flow-version` — single-line stamp, first line = `__version__`

Root `CLAUDE.md` is a lightweight project-context file and does NOT carry a version — do not add version frontmatter or banners to it. After bumping, also re-run `make sync-human-docs` to propagate the new version into generated docs. If you edit `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` or any reference/example outside of a version bump, run `make sync-cursor-skill` before committing so the mirror stays current.

## Rule CP-4 — Gate Module Changes

Changes to `src/devolaflow/gate/` require running the full gate test suite:
```
python -m pytest tests/test_gate.py -v
```

## Rule CP-5 — SKILL Changes Require Adapter Build

Changes to SKILL.md, CLAUDE.md, or workflow-skill.yaml require running `build-skill` and verifying all 4 adapter outputs (Cursor, Codex, Claude, Copilot) build successfully and stay within their budgets.

## Rule CP-6 — Context Optimization Changes Require Benchmarks

Changes to `task_adaptive_selector.py`, `context_profiles.yaml`, or lean message schemas require running the EvoBench benchmark suite:
```
python -m pytest tests/test_benchmarks.py -v
```

## Rule CP-7 — Pre-Commit Verification Checklist

Before committing to this repository, verify:
1. `python -m pytest tests/ -q` — all tests pass
2. `ruff check src/ tests/` — no lint errors
3. `ruff format --check src/ tests/` — formatting correct
4. No absolute filesystem paths introduced in agent-facing files
5. CHANGELOG updated if user-visible changes were made
